sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Patient / Clinician
    participant UI as React Frontend (App.tsx)
    participant API as FastAPI (backend/main.py)
    participant RS as ReportService (src/report_service.py)
    participant Ollama as Ollama Runtime (medgemma:4b)
    participant Triage as TriageService (src/triage_service.py)

    User->>UI: Uploads full radiograph and enters reason for X-ray
    UI->>API: POST /report/patient-friendly (Multipart: file, reason, history)
    API->>API: _validate_upload() (< 50MB, DICOM/PNG/JPG)
    API->>RS: patient_friendly_report(image_bytes, reason, history)
    RS->>RS: _load_to_rgb_array() & resize to max_side=1024 (LANCZOS)
    RS->>RS: _array_to_base64_jpeg() (Quality=85)
    
    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        note over RS,Ollama: Stage 1: Objective Visual Feature Extraction
        RS->>Ollama: POST /api/generate (Images: [full_b64], Prompt: "Describe visible abnormalities/densities", num_predict=130)
        Ollama-->>RS: raw_obs: "Bilateral lower lung opacities, heart size normal..."
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 240)
        note over RS,Ollama: Stage 2: Patient-Friendly Structuring & Translation
        RS->>Ollama: POST /api/generate (Prompt: "Translate observed findings into 4 sections", num_predict=180)
        Ollama-->>RS: raw_text (draft headings)
    end

    RS->>RS: clean_and_structure_patient_report():
    RS->>RS: Intercepts & replaces "only shows one side" fallacy
    RS->>RS: Strips leaked disclaimers & validates numerical units
    
    RS->>Triage: evaluate_from_report_text(full_text, sections)
    Triage->>Triage: Evaluates YAML rules with negation cues and contradiction checks
    Triage-->>RS: TriageEvaluationResult (category, matched rule, review priority)
    
    RS-->>API: Result dict with report_text, sections, triage_result, timing
    API-->>UI: PatientFriendlyReportResponse (JSON)
    UI->>User: Renders 4 structured cards, research triage banner, and disclaimers
